@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] native-file-lock-keeps-bsd-semantics
The native bridge MUST pass the caller's file descriptor and flags unchanged to BSD
flock and return its actual status without changing errno. It MUST NOT substitute
process-scoped fcntl locks or add waiting/retry behavior. Swift MUST retain ownership
of nonblocking acquisition, EINTR/error handling and release on that same descriptor.
Source: ios-share-record-coordinates-real-processes, ios-share-lock-contention-does-not-block-the-host
